# Testing

After substantive code changes, run and **read** the output of:

- `pnpm verify:fast` (or `verify:fast:quiet`) for local loops and pre-push (Lefthook)
- Targeted e2e: `pnpm test:e2e:changed:quiet` once when green (same target set as CI burn-in). Full `pnpm test:e2e:quiet` / `pnpm test:e2e` / `pnpm verify` only when needed for the Verification checklist; out-of-scope failures per `docs/roadmap/RULES.md` Agent apply hygiene. Flake proof is CI burn-in, not local repeats — local `--repeat-each=3` only if a specific spec failed locally then passed on rerun. Playwright also gates every PR in CI

Also available:

- `pnpm stryker:diff` — mutations on files changed vs `origin/main`
- `pnpm test:lhci` — Lighthouse CI against `budget.json`
- `pnpm bench` — vitest bench

PBT: use `@fast-check/vitest`; default `numRuns` ~100 locally; CI may raise via `FC_NUM_RUNS`.

Test authorship conventions: skill `write-tests` (mandates in `openspec/config.yaml` quality bar).
